; /XTRA
;; overlay.ab3 -- the back playfield brought in front, as an overlay for the title and the
;; options (the title-overlay plan, step 1).
;; Compile in UAE. Not part of the game. Built on band-split.ab3: the same two lists (the HUD
;; band over the dual-playfield world, fetch mode 3, DisplayAdjust -1 and -1, PF2OF 16) and
;; the same band split by poked copper strings.
;;
;; Three things are new here:
;; 1. PF2PRI. BPLCON2's bit 6 puts playfield 2, the back, in front of playfield 1. The
;;    library's BPLCON2 is $224, so DisplayControls 1, $40, 0, 0 should set PF2PRI and
;;    leave PF2OF at 16. Called at run time (line-scroll.ab3 proved a run-time call for
;;    BPLCON3).
;;    After each call the band strings are checked again: if the call rebuilt the list and
;;    the strings are gone, the band falls back to CustomString and the results file says so.
;; 2. A double-buffered canvas on the back bitmap: two 384 px pages side by side, at x 0 and
;;    x 384. A change is drawn on the hidden page, then DisplayBitMap shows it by its x. The
;;    band split shows the same page below #BAND_LINE: the hills' x is the page's x.
;; 3. The cover under the overlay: the front shows a blank bitmap with entry 0 black, as the
;;    options screen will.
;;
;; The front scrolls right at 1 px a frame with the bob load, as the attract mode will. The
;; overlay is boxes standing in for the title: a logo block, three menu lines and a cursor.
;; Keys:
;;   O         the overlay on and off. Off, the back is the clouds and hills again (redrawn,
;;             so they may show half drawn for a frame or two: the game does this behind a
;;             cover)
;;   Up, Down  move the cursor (one redraw of the page)
;;   Space     redraw the page every frame, with a bar that grows (the worst case)
;;   B         draw on the shown page instead of the hidden one (today's title, which
;;             flickers): a red box in the HUD means single buffered
;;   C         the cover under the overlay on and off (a bright yellow box in the HUD)
;;   Esc       quit and write overlay-results.txt
;;
;; First run (2026-10-15): the overlay came to the front and lined up across the band line,
;; the world showed through its pen 0, no flicker double buffered, and the band strings
;; survived 11 run-time DisplayControls calls. A page redraw took 168 lines (the whole page
;; cleared and drawn again). But the overlay was yellow, not blue: its colours were at
;; entries 8 to 15. The library's _dobplcons (displaylib.ab3) XORs each argument with the
;; register's CURRENT value in the list, not with the default the manual gives: the start's
;; $1c00 made BPLCON3 $1000 (PF2OF 16), and the overlay's $1c00 XORed it back to $c00
;; (PF2OF 8). So DisplayControls is a toggle at run time: the overlay now flips PF2PRI with
;; DisplayControls 1, $40, 0, 0, the same call on and off. Also on the first run, C did not
;; turn the screen black.
;;
;; Third run (2026-10-15, in the game): on the NTSC build the title overlay moved left and right
;; a pixel as the level scrolled behind it; on PAL it did not. The NTSC attract mode steps the
;; camera 213/256 px a tick, PAL a whole pixel, and the runs above only moved the front by whole
;; pixels. Two keys to find which it is:
;;   F         the front's speed: 1 px a frame, or 213/256 px (the NTSC attract mode's). A red
;;             box at the HUD's left means the fractional speed.
;;   U         stop and restart the band split's pokes (the overlay below the stripe then keeps
;;             the last value: a dark red box at the HUD's left means stopped)
;; Report: with F (fractional), on the PAL profile and on the NTSC profile, does the overlay move?
;; All of it, or only below the stripe (the band line)? And with U as well, does it stop?
;; Fourth run: it moved on NTSC only, and only with F; but on NTSC the HUD was corrupt and a HUD box
;; out of place, because the lists started at line 44, PAL's, and ran past NTSC's last line. Now
;; they start at 32 on NTSC, as the game's do, and the NTSC result needs taking again.
;; Fifth run: the display solid on NTSC. F moves the overlay on both PAL and NTSC; with F off it is
;; steady on both. So the front's fraction is the trigger, not NTSC (the game's PAL attract mode
;; stepped whole pixels).
;; Sixth run: with F all of the overlay moves; with U as well, the part below the stripe is steady
;; and the part above still moves. Both writers of BPLCON1 (the library above the band line, the
;; poked string below it) give it, with the back's bits unchanged: the display moves the back when
;; only the front's sub-pixel bits change (the emulator or the chips), not this code.

;; What to look at and report
;; 1. With O: the boxes in front of the pillars and the ground; the pillars and ground show
;;    wherever the overlay has pen 0 (the overlay's pen 0 is transparent, the hole in the
;;    logo block too); the HUD band and its colours unchanged.
;; 2. The overlay's lower part (below the stripe about a third of the way down, the band
;;    line) lines up with the upper part: no step sideways, no torn line.
;; 3. Up, Down and Space: no flicker, no half-drawn page. Then B and Space: the flicker, for
;;    comparison.
;; 4. O again: the clouds and hills back behind the pillars, the band split working (the
;;    hills slower than the front, the clouds slower still).
;; 5. C with the overlay on: black behind the boxes, nothing of the world showing.
;; 6. The results file: whether the band strings survived the DisplayControls calls, and the
;;    page redraw's lines.

WBStartup

;; =======================================================
;; CONSTANTS
;; =======================================================

#RAW_KEY_O     = $18
#RAW_KEY_C     = $33
#RAW_KEY_B     = $35
#RAW_KEY_SPACE = $40
#RAW_KEY_ESC   = $45
#RAW_KEY_UP    = $4C
#RAW_KEY_DOWN  = $4D
#RAW_KEY_U     = $16
#RAW_KEY_F     = $23

;; The CopList object (displaylib.ab3, NEWTYPE .mycop): the pointer to its custom copper
;; area is the eighth long. The byte offsets of the strings' value words, from customs.
#POKE_FIRST    = 10
#MYCOP_CUSTOMS = 28
#POKE_SECOND   = 34

;; The hills' x in quarter pixels, less the fine part: changes once every 64 px.
#HILL_BLOCK_MASK = $FF00

#LIST_GAP   = 3
#HUD_H      = 16
#COPPER_COLORS = 32
#VIEW_TOP   = 32
;; The lists' first line: 44 on a PAL machine, 32 on NTSC, as the game (constants.ab3,
;; #HUD_YPOS_PAL and _NTSC; proofs/ntsc-lines.ab3: from 36 down the picture runs past NTSC's last
;; line). The proof's first NTSC run used 44 and its HUD came out corrupt.
#HUD_YPOS_PAL  = 44
#HUD_YPOS_NTSC = 32
#VIEW_H     = 208
#VIEW_W     = 320

#HUD_FLAGS   = $13014
#WORLD_FLAGS = $13038

#STRING_B_SLOT = 6
#BAND_CUSTOMS  = 13

;; DisplayControls XORs each register with its current value in the list: this flips PF2PRI
;; (BPLCON2 bit 6), the back in front, on and off again.
#PLAYFIELD2_PRIORITY = $40
;; BPLCON3 is the library default $c00 XOR this: PF2OF 16 rather than 8.
#PLAYFIELD2_OFFSET_16 = $1c00

#DISPLAY_ADJUST_START = -1
#DISPLAY_ADJUST_STOP  = -1

;; Bitmaps: 0 and 1 the front pair, 2 the back, 3 the HUD band, 4 the shape source, 5 the cover.
#BM_A       = 0
#BM_B       = 1
#BM_BACK    = 2
#BM_HUD     = 3
#BM_SHAPE   = 4
#BM_COVER   = 5
#WORLD_H    = 256
#HUD_W      = 384
#FRONT_WRAP = 512
#PERIOD     = 768
#FRONT_W    = 1024
#BACK_W     = 1152

;; The two pages of the canvas, each the view plus the fetch guard.
#PAGE_W = 384

#BAND_LINE = 80

#BPL2PTH = $E4
#BPL4PTH = $EC
#BPL6PTH = $F4
#BPL8PTH = $FC
#BPLCON1 = $102

#BOB_SHAPE = 0
#TILE      = 16
#BOB_BYTES = 16384

#MENU_LINES = 3
#BOBS       = 8
#WORK_LINE  = 80
#LINES_PAL  = 312

;; =======================================================
;; GLOBALS
;; =======================================================

quitFlag.w = False
drawBm.w = #BM_B
drawBuf.w = 1
frameCount.l = 0
cameraX.q = 0
frontX.q = 0
cloudX.q = 0
hillX.q = 0
viewX.w = 0
startLine.l = 0
endLine.l = 0
backBytesPerRow.l = 0
copListAddress.l = 0
customsAddress.l = 0
pokeMode.w = False
overlayOn.w = False
coverOn.w = False
singleBuffer.w = False
animateOn.w = False
pageDirty.w = False
shownPage.w = 0
pageToShow.w = 0
cursorLine.w = 0
oWasDown.w = False
cWasDown.w = False
bWasDown.w = False
spaceWasDown.w = False
upWasDown.w = False
downWasDown.w = False
fractionalSpeed.w = False
fWasDown.w = False
bandFrozen.w = False
uWasDown.w = False
controlCalls.l = 0
stringsLost.l = 0
redrawCount.l = 0
redrawLines.l = 0
redrawSum.l = 0
redrawMax.l = 0

Dim backPlane.l(3)
Dim frontScrollPart.l(255)
Dim backScrollPart.l(255)
lastHillBlock.l = -1

;; =======================================================
;; ALLOC (AMIGA MODE)
;; =======================================================

BitMap #BM_A, #FRONT_W, #WORLD_H, 4
BitMap #BM_B, #FRONT_W, #WORLD_H, 4
BitMap #BM_BACK, #BACK_W, #WORLD_H, 4
BitMap #BM_HUD, #HUD_W, #HUD_H, 4
BitMap #BM_SHAPE, 16, #TILE, 4
BitMap #BM_COVER, #PAGE_W, #WORLD_H, 4

backBytesPerRow = Peek.w(Addr BitMap(#BM_BACK))
For planeIndex.w = 0 To 3
  backPlane(planeIndex) = Peek.l(Addr BitMap(#BM_BACK) + 8 + planeIndex*4)
Next

;; 0 the sky; 1 to 7 reds; 8 to 15 yellows; 16 black; 17 to 23 blues; 24 to 31 greys.
InitPalette 0, #COPPER_COLORS
AGAPalRGB 0, 0, 92, 148, 252
For colourIndex.w = 1 To 7
  AGAPalRGB 0, colourIndex, 100 + colourIndex*22, 0, 0
  AGAPalRGB 0, colourIndex + 8, 100 + colourIndex*22, 100 + colourIndex*22, 0
  AGAPalRGB 0, colourIndex + 16, 0, 0, 100 + colourIndex*22
  AGAPalRGB 0, colourIndex + 24, 60 + colourIndex*25, 60 + colourIndex*25, 60 + colourIndex*25
Next
AGAPalRGB 0, 8, 255, 255, 0
AGAPalRGB 0, 16, 0, 0, 0
AGAPalRGB 0, 24, 40, 40, 40

;; =======================================================
;; DISPLAY (BLITZ MODE)
;; =======================================================

; The machine's standard, read in Amiga mode (as init.ab3 does): False on PAL, True on NTSC.
videoIsNtsc.w = NTSC
hudLine.w = #HUD_YPOS_PAL
If videoIsNtsc = True Then hudLine = #HUD_YPOS_NTSC

BLITZ

Buffer 0, #BOB_BYTES
Buffer 1, #BOB_BYTES

;; Beam line: VPOSR bit 0 is V8, VHPOSR high byte V0 to V7.
Function.l RasterLine{}
  rawPosition.l = Peek.l($dff004)
  Function Return (rawPosition AND $1ff00)/256
End Function

; A 16 bit value as the signed word Mki$ and Poke.w take.
Function.l SignedWord{value.l}
  value = value AND $ffff
  If value > 32767 Then value = value - 65536
  Function Return value
End Function

;; One playfield's part of BPLCON1 for a delay of 0 to 255 quarter pixels, in the
;; playfield 1 bits. Playfield 2's part is this times 16.
Function.l ScrollPart{delay.l}
  Function Return (delay AND 3)*256 + ((delay/4) AND 15) + ((delay/64) AND 3)*1024
End Function

;; The two copper strings at the band line, built from scratch (band-split.ab3).
Statement UpdateBand{}
  SHARED frontX, hillX, backPlane(), backBytesPerRow
  frontQuarter.l = Int(frontX*4)
  hillQuarter.l = Int(hillX*4)
  control.l = ScrollPart{255 - (frontQuarter AND 255)} + ScrollPart{255 - (hillQuarter AND 255)}*16
  coarseBytes.l = (hillQuarter/256)*8
  rowStart.l = (#VIEW_TOP + #BAND_LINE - 1)*backBytesPerRow + coarseBytes
  pointer0.l = backPlane(0) + rowStart
  pointer1.l = backPlane(1) + rowStart
  firstString$ = Mki$(#BPL2PTH) + Mki$(SignedWord{pointer0/65536}) + Mki$(#BPL2PTH + 2) + Mki$(SignedWord{pointer0})
  firstString$ = firstString$ + Mki$(#BPL4PTH) + Mki$(SignedWord{pointer1/65536}) + Mki$(#BPL4PTH + 2) + Mki$(SignedWord{pointer1})
  rowStart = rowStart + backBytesPerRow
  pointer2.l = backPlane(2) + rowStart
  pointer3.l = backPlane(3) + rowStart
  secondString$ = Mki$(#BPL6PTH) + Mki$(SignedWord{pointer2/65536}) + Mki$(#BPL6PTH + 2) + Mki$(SignedWord{pointer2})
  secondString$ = secondString$ + Mki$(#BPL8PTH) + Mki$(SignedWord{pointer3/65536}) + Mki$(#BPL8PTH + 2) + Mki$(SignedWord{pointer3})
  secondString$ = secondString$ + Mki$(#BPLCON1) + Mki$(SignedWord{control})
  CustomString 1, 0, #BAND_LINE - 2, firstString$
  CustomString 1, #STRING_B_SLOT, #BAND_LINE - 1, secondString$
End Statement

Statement PokeBandPointers{hillQuarter.l}
  SHARED backPlane(), backBytesPerRow, customsAddress
  rowStart.l = (#VIEW_TOP + #BAND_LINE - 1)*backBytesPerRow + (hillQuarter/256)*8
  pointer.l = backPlane(0) + rowStart
  Poke.w customsAddress + #POKE_FIRST, SignedWord{pointer/65536}
  Poke.w customsAddress + #POKE_FIRST + 4, SignedWord{pointer}
  pointer = backPlane(1) + rowStart
  Poke.w customsAddress + #POKE_FIRST + 8, SignedWord{pointer/65536}
  Poke.w customsAddress + #POKE_FIRST + 12, SignedWord{pointer}
  rowStart = rowStart + backBytesPerRow
  pointer = backPlane(2) + rowStart
  Poke.w customsAddress + #POKE_SECOND, SignedWord{pointer/65536}
  Poke.w customsAddress + #POKE_SECOND + 4, SignedWord{pointer}
  pointer = backPlane(3) + rowStart
  Poke.w customsAddress + #POKE_SECOND + 8, SignedWord{pointer/65536}
  Poke.w customsAddress + #POKE_SECOND + 12, SignedWord{pointer}
End Statement

Statement PokeBand{}
  SHARED frontX, hillX, customsAddress, lastHillBlock, frontScrollPart(), backScrollPart()
  frontQuarter.l = Int(frontX*4)
  hillQuarter.l = Int(hillX*4)
  control.l = frontScrollPart(frontQuarter AND 255) + backScrollPart(hillQuarter AND 255)
  Poke.w customsAddress + #POKE_SECOND + 16, SignedWord{control}
  hillBlock.l = hillQuarter AND #HILL_BLOCK_MASK
  If hillBlock <> lastHillBlock
    lastHillBlock = hillBlock
    PokeBandPointers{hillQuarter}
  EndIf
End Statement

Statement BuildScrollTables{}
  SHARED frontScrollPart(), backScrollPart()
  For fineIndex.w = 0 To 255
    frontScrollPart(fineIndex) = ScrollPart{255 - fineIndex}
    backScrollPart(fineIndex) = ScrollPart{255 - fineIndex}*16
  Next
End Statement

;; The poke path is used only while both strings' first register words are where the
;; layout puts them. Checked at start and after every DisplayControls call; strings found
;; missing after a call are counted. lastHillBlock is cleared so the pointers are poked again.
Statement CheckBandStrings{}
  SHARED copListAddress, customsAddress, pokeMode, stringsLost, controlCalls, lastHillBlock
  wasPoking.w = pokeMode
  pokeMode = False
  copListAddress = Addr CopList(1)
  customsAddress = Peek.l(copListAddress + #MYCOP_CUSTOMS)
  If customsAddress <> 0
    If Peek.w(customsAddress + #POKE_FIRST - 2) = #BPL2PTH
      If Peek.w(customsAddress + #POKE_SECOND - 2) = #BPL6PTH Then pokeMode = True
    EndIf
  EndIf
  If controlCalls > 0 AND wasPoking = True AND pokeMode = False Then stringsLost = stringsLost + 1
  lastHillBlock = -1
End Statement

;; The HUD: a red box for single buffered, a bright yellow box for the cover, a dull yellow
;; box while the overlay is on.
Statement DrawHud{}
  SHARED singleBuffer, coverOn, overlayOn, fractionalSpeed, bandFrozen
  Use BitMap #BM_HUD
  Cls 0
  If singleBuffer = True Then Boxf 296, 4, 303, 11, 4
  If coverOn = True Then Boxf 284, 4, 291, 11, 15
  If overlayOn = True Then Boxf 272, 4, 279, 11, 10
  If fractionalSpeed = True Then Boxf 8, 4, 15, 11, 4
  If bandFrozen = True Then Boxf 20, 4, 27, 11, 2
End Statement

;; The front: ground in pens 1 and 2, a tall pillar in pen 3 every 128 px.
Statement DrawFront{bitmapIndex.w}
  Use BitMap bitmapIndex
  Cls 0
  For columnIndex.w = 0 To #FRONT_W/#TILE - 1
    pen.w = 1
    If columnIndex MOD 2 = 1 Then pen = 2
    Boxf columnIndex*#TILE, 208, columnIndex*#TILE + #TILE - 1, 239, pen
  Next
  For pillarX.w = 48 To #FRONT_W - 64 Step 128
    Boxf pillarX, 40, pillarX + 23, 207, 3
  Next
End Statement

Statement DrawBackPiece{pieceX.w}
  Boxf pieceX + 16, 48, pieceX + 111, 79, 5
  Boxf pieceX + 32, 40, pieceX + 79, 47, 5
  Boxf pieceX + 120, 160, pieceX + 183, 207, 6
  Boxf pieceX + 136, 140, pieceX + 167, 159, 6
End Statement

;; The clouds and hills, as the game's StampBackPlayfield{} puts them back after the overlay.
Statement DrawBack{}
  Use BitMap #BM_BACK
  Cls 0
  For pieceX.w = 0 To #BACK_W - 192 Step 192
    DrawBackPiece{pieceX}
  Next
  Boxf 0, 36, 3, 95, 7
  Boxf #PERIOD, 36, #PERIOD + 3, 95, 7
  Boxf 0, 128, 3, 207, 7
  Boxf #PERIOD, 128, #PERIOD + 3, 207, 7
End Statement

;; One page of the overlay at x pageX of the back bitmap, cleared to pen 0 first. The logo
;; block where the title's logo sits (176 x 88 from row 48), with a hole of pen 0 through
;; it, a stripe across the band line so a step there shows, three menu lines, the cursor
;; and, while Space is on, a bar that grows a pixel a frame.
Statement DrawPage{pageX.w}
  SHARED cursorLine, animateOn, frameCount
  Use BitMap #BM_BACK
  Boxf pageX, #VIEW_TOP, pageX + #PAGE_W - 1, #VIEW_TOP + #VIEW_H - 1, 0
  Boxf pageX + 72, 48, pageX + 247, 135, 3
  Boxf pageX + 80, 56, pageX + 239, 127, 2
  Boxf pageX + 136, 72, pageX + 183, 111, 0
  Boxf pageX + 16, #VIEW_TOP + #BAND_LINE - 4, pageX + 303, #VIEW_TOP + #BAND_LINE + 3, 6
  For lineIndex.w = 0 To #MENU_LINES - 1
    Boxf pageX + 112, 160 + lineIndex*16, pageX + 223 - lineIndex*16, 167 + lineIndex*16, 7
  Next
  Boxf pageX + 96, 160 + cursorLine*16, pageX + 103, 167 + cursorLine*16, 5
  If animateOn = True
    Boxf pageX + 80, 216, pageX + 80 + (frameCount MOD 160), 223, 4
  EndIf
End Statement

Statement MakeShapes{}
  Use BitMap #BM_SHAPE
  Cls 0
  Circlef 7, 7, 7, 4
  Circlef 7, 7, 3, 7
  GetaShape #BOB_SHAPE, 0, 0, #TILE, #TILE
End Statement

BBlitMode CookieMode
MakeShapes{}
DrawFront{#BM_A}
DrawFront{#BM_B}
DrawBack{}
DrawHud{}
Use BitMap #BM_COVER
Cls 0

InitCopList 0, hudLine, #HUD_H, #HUD_FLAGS, 0, #COPPER_COLORS, 0
InitCopList 1, hudLine + #HUD_H + #LIST_GAP, #VIEW_H, #WORLD_FLAGS, 0, 0, #BAND_CUSTOMS
DisplayAdjust 0, 0, 0, 0, #DISPLAY_ADJUST_START, #DISPLAY_ADJUST_STOP
DisplayAdjust 1, 0, 0, 0, #DISPLAY_ADJUST_START, #DISPLAY_ADJUST_STOP
DisplayControls 1, 0, #PLAYFIELD2_OFFSET_16, 0
CreateDisplay 0, 1
DisplayPalette 0, 0
DisplayBitMap 0, #BM_HUD, 0, 0
DisplayBitMap 1, drawBm, 0, #VIEW_TOP, #BM_BACK, 0, #VIEW_TOP
BuildScrollTables{}
UpdateBand{}
CheckBandStrings{}
BlitzKeys On

While quitFlag = False
  If RawStatus(#RAW_KEY_ESC) Then quitFlag = True

  ;; O: the overlay. On, both pages are drawn before the back comes to the front, so the
  ;; first frame shows a whole page. Off, the back goes behind, then the strip is redrawn.
  If RawStatus(#RAW_KEY_O)
    If oWasDown = False
      overlayOn = NOT overlayOn
      If overlayOn = True
        DrawPage{0}
        DrawPage{#PAGE_W}
        shownPage = 0
        pageToShow = 0
        VWait
        DisplayControls 1, #PLAYFIELD2_PRIORITY, 0, 0
      Else
        coverOn = False
        AGAPalRGB 0, 0, 92, 148, 252
        DisplayPalette 0, 0
        VWait
        DisplayControls 1, #PLAYFIELD2_PRIORITY, 0, 0
        DrawBack{}
      EndIf
      controlCalls = controlCalls + 1
      CheckBandStrings{}
      DrawHud{}
    EndIf
    oWasDown = True
  Else
    oWasDown = False
  EndIf

  ;; C: the cover under the overlay, the front blank with entry 0 black.
  If RawStatus(#RAW_KEY_C)
    If cWasDown = False AND overlayOn = True
      coverOn = NOT coverOn
      If coverOn = True
        AGAPalRGB 0, 0, 0, 0, 0
      Else
        AGAPalRGB 0, 0, 92, 148, 252
      EndIf
      DisplayPalette 0, 0
      DrawHud{}
    EndIf
    cWasDown = True
  Else
    cWasDown = False
  EndIf

  If RawStatus(#RAW_KEY_B)
    If bWasDown = False
      singleBuffer = NOT singleBuffer
      DrawHud{}
    EndIf
    bWasDown = True
  Else
    bWasDown = False
  EndIf

  If RawStatus(#RAW_KEY_SPACE)
    If spaceWasDown = False
      animateOn = NOT animateOn
      pageDirty = True
    EndIf
    spaceWasDown = True
  Else
    spaceWasDown = False
  EndIf

  If RawStatus(#RAW_KEY_UP)
    If upWasDown = False AND cursorLine > 0
      cursorLine = cursorLine - 1
      pageDirty = True
    EndIf
    upWasDown = True
  Else
    upWasDown = False
  EndIf
  If RawStatus(#RAW_KEY_DOWN)
    If downWasDown = False AND cursorLine < #MENU_LINES - 1
      cursorLine = cursorLine + 1
      pageDirty = True
    EndIf
    downWasDown = True
  Else
    downWasDown = False
  EndIf
  If animateOn = True Then pageDirty = True

  If RawStatus(#RAW_KEY_F)
    If fWasDown = False
      fractionalSpeed = NOT fractionalSpeed
      DrawHud{}
    EndIf
    fWasDown = True
  Else
    fWasDown = False
  EndIf
  If RawStatus(#RAW_KEY_U)
    If uWasDown = False
      bandFrozen = NOT bandFrozen
      DrawHud{}
    EndIf
    uWasDown = True
  Else
    uWasDown = False
  EndIf

  ;; The front scrolls right at 1 px a frame (or 213/256, F); the clouds at a quarter, the hills at half.
  If fractionalSpeed = True
    cameraX = cameraX + 213*0.00390625
  Else
    cameraX = cameraX + 1
  EndIf
  If cameraX >= #PERIOD*4 Then cameraX = cameraX - #PERIOD*4
  frontX = cameraX
  While frontX >= #FRONT_WRAP
    frontX = frontX - #FRONT_WRAP
  Wend
  cloudX = cameraX/4
  While cloudX >= #PERIOD
    cloudX = cloudX - #PERIOD
  Wend
  hillX = cameraX/2
  While hillX >= #PERIOD
    hillX = hillX - #PERIOD
  Wend
  viewX = Int(frontX)

  While RasterLine{} < #WORK_LINE
  Wend
  Use BitMap drawBm
  UnBuffer drawBuf
  For bobIndex.w = 0 To #BOBS - 1
    BBlit drawBuf, #BOB_SHAPE, viewX + 20 + bobIndex*36, 112 + (bobIndex MOD 2)*48
  Next

  ;; A changed page: on the hidden page, shown after the VWait; or, single buffered, on the
  ;; shown page while it is being displayed.
  pageToShow = shownPage
  If overlayOn = True AND pageDirty = True
    startLine = RasterLine{}
    If singleBuffer = True
      DrawPage{shownPage*#PAGE_W}
    Else
      pageToShow = 1 - shownPage
      DrawPage{pageToShow*#PAGE_W}
    EndIf
    endLine = RasterLine{}
    redrawLines = endLine - startLine
    If redrawLines < 0 Then redrawLines = redrawLines + #LINES_PAL
    redrawCount = redrawCount + 1
    redrawSum = redrawSum + redrawLines
    If redrawLines > redrawMax Then redrawMax = redrawLines
    pageDirty = False
  EndIf

  VWait
  If overlayOn = True
    shownPage = pageToShow
    ;; The canvas does not scroll: both bands at the page's x.
    cloudX = shownPage*#PAGE_W
    hillX = cloudX
  EndIf
  If coverOn = True
    frontX = 0
    DisplayBitMap 1, #BM_COVER, 0, #VIEW_TOP, #BM_BACK, cloudX, #VIEW_TOP
  Else
    DisplayBitMap 1, drawBm, frontX, #VIEW_TOP, #BM_BACK, cloudX, #VIEW_TOP
  EndIf
  If bandFrozen = False
    If pokeMode = True
      PokeBand{}
    Else
      UpdateBand{}
    EndIf
  EndIf

  If drawBm = #BM_A
    drawBm = #BM_B
    drawBuf = 1
  Else
    drawBm = #BM_A
    drawBuf = 0
  EndIf
  frameCount = frameCount + 1
Wend

AMIGA
If WriteFile(0, "sparky-dave:game/proofs/results/overlay-results.txt")
  FileOutput 0
  NPrint "overlay: HUD $", Hex$(#HUD_FLAGS), ", world $", Hex$(#WORLD_FLAGS), ", customs ", #BAND_CUSTOMS, ", ", frameCount, " frames"
  NPrint "DisplayControls calls at run time: ", controlCalls, ", band strings lost after one: ", stringsLost
  If pokeMode = True
    NPrint "band update at exit: by poking the copper list (customs at $", Hex$(customsAddress), ")"
  Else
    NPrint "band update at exit: by CustomString, the poke check failed (CopList at $", Hex$(copListAddress), ", customs read as $", Hex$(customsAddress), ")"
  EndIf
  If redrawCount > 0
    NPrint "page redraws: ", redrawCount, ", average lines ", redrawSum/redrawCount, ", worst ", redrawMax
  Else
    NPrint "page redraws: none (the overlay was never changed while on)"
  EndIf
  NPrint ""
  NPrint "The picture is the main result: report the six points at the top of the proof."
  CloseFile 0
EndIf
End
